description:
Delete `:rf.warning/machine-source-unstamped`. It is a dev warning that fires on legal machine registrations.

## What it does

`maybe-warn-source-unstamped!` in `implementation/machines/src/re_frame/machines/lifecycle_fx/registration.cljc` (called under `debug-enabled?`) warns whenever a machine spec arrives without source metadata. That includes:
- the legal `(def m {…}) (reg-machine :id m)` shape;
- every runtime-built spec;
- a literal whose only fn is a symbol.

## Why it should go

The warning's own message tells runtime-built authors they "may ignore this advisory". No other registration kind warns when source coordinates are missing. It has already needed a JVM false-positive fix (rf2-hefqg). The project rule is to warn on failures, not on legal code.

## Change

Delete:
- the warning and its `source-unstamped-warned` atom;
- `clear-source-unstamped-warned!`, `spec-carries-source-metadata?` and `spec-carries-fn?`;
