## Ruling

The app-facing handled-event sink record, `:rf.observe/handled-event`, takes the names the event tap record already uses:
- `:status` becomes `:outcome`, with the same value set (`:ok | :error | :rolled-back | :flow-error | :rejected`);
- it gains `:time`, the router's existing `end-ms` for that event.

After this, the tap record, the handled-event sink record and the sink's error record agree: one name for each fact, and all three carry `:time`. This is an app-facing rename, and pre-alpha is the cheap time to remove the mismatch. It changes only those two fields. An app's `configure!` and `register-observability-sink!` code is unchanged.

